# Generated by just contracts from genie-model's types (FD-046-D15). Do not edit.
{
  ActionKind | doc "An action type: a task's `action_type` (`+0x10`, the `.dat`'s) and an action's type (`+0x8`),\none numbering. The `.dat` holds types the simulation does not run (the AI's, the scenario's),\nso the type is a newtype with named constants, not an enum: any value 0 or more the data\nholds is a type, and the named ones are values of the type. A field or a filter that holds −1\nfor none or any is `Option<ActionKind>`." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && -32768 <= x && x <= 32767),
  ActionPart | doc "The action layer of a master of type 40 and up but 90 (`RGE_Master_Action_Object`,\n`+0x790`..`+0x7b9`; the `.dat`'s type-40 section, genieutils' `Bird`): its tasks and the default\none, its task swap group, its work rate, its search radius, its drop sites and its run pattern.\nAn action unit (40), a combat master (50), a missile (60), a combat unit (70) and a building\n(80) hold it." = {
    task_by_group | TaskGroup | doc "`+0x7b8`, the `.dat`'s `TaskSwapGroup` (the save does not carry it); 0 for none.",
    tasks | Array (Task) | doc "Its task list.",
