    amount | Number | doc "The fourth.",
    mode | ChangeMode | doc "The third argument's low byte.",
  }), 'TechDisable ({
    tech | DisabledTech | doc "The fourth argument as CVTTSS2SI gives it.",
  }), 'TechTime ({
    tech | TechId | optional | doc "The first argument (a negative one is none).",
    amount | Number | doc "The fourth.",
    mode | ChangeMode | doc "The third argument's low byte.",
  }), 'Inert (std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && 0 <= x && x <= 255)) |],
  EffectId | doc "An effect's id: its place in the world's effect table (`+0x128`), as a technology (`+0x3a`) and\na player's effect override (`+0x62`) hold it, −1 for none. Every short is kept.\nThe default is 0, as a zeroed record holds it." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && -32768 <= x && x <= 32767),
  ExploreTuning | doc "The `explore` port's tuning values." = {
    los_margin | Number | doc "The auto scout's search reaches within its line of sight less this (`FUN_140c65490`, `DAT_14330eb8c`).\n\n`explore::LOS_MARGIN`: 1 in build 158041.",
  },
  FacetCount | doc "A graphic's facet count (`angle_count`, `+0xa`, a short): how many directions it draws.\nEvery value is kept." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && -32768 <= x && x <= 32767),
  Firepower | doc "A firepower: the missiles a volley fires (a float: a master's `volley_fire_amount`, `+0x8c0`,\nwhich the effects set, add to and scale; an object's `+0xa00`, its master's plus the shares\nof the units inside it). Each operator is the one `f32` operation the game does; every value\nis kept." = Number,
  FlyMode | doc "A master's fly mode (`+0x608`, the `.dat`'s `fly_mode`): where an object's height goes against\nthe ground's (`FUN_141193a10`, `genie_core::combat::missile::grounded`). Every byte is kept; one\nnot named keeps its height." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && 0 <= x && x <= 255),
  FlyTuning | doc "The `fly` port's tuning values." = {
    height | Number | doc "The height a bird of fly mode 1 flies at once its Fly starts (`FUN_140a84900`).\n\n`fly::HEIGHT`: 9 in build 158041.",
  },
  FogVisibility | doc "A master's fog visibility (`+0x605`, the `.dat`'s `fog_visibility`; openage's names): an Attack\ngoes on against an object of any but [`FogVisibility::INVISIBLE`] in the fog. Every byte is\nkept." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && 0 <= x && x <= 255),
  Footprint | doc "An object's radii on the ground: x and y in tiles, half its size along each axis (a master's\n`radius_x` and `radius_y`, `+0x5d8`, `+0x5dc`). The area it covers is its place plus and minus\nthem." = Array (Number),
  FormationClass | doc "A master's formation category (`mFormationCategory`, `+0x8bc`): which sub-formation of a group\nits units take (`genie_core::groups::sub_formation`: 1 to 4 their own, 0 and 5 the protected one,\n6 the first). 0 keeps a unit out of the groups an order's splitter forms (`FUN_140fd76d0`).\nEvery byte is kept." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && 0 <= x && x <= 255),
  Frame | doc "A frame of a sprite (a short): the frame a sprite shows (`+0x24`) and showed before\n(`+0x30`), a graphic's frame count (`frame_count`, `+0x8`, one past its last frame), a\nmaster's fire and interrupt frames and the frame a BUILD command chose. Each operator is the\ngame's 16-bit one; every value is kept." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && -32768 <= x && x <= 32767),
  GarrisonCapacity | doc "A master's garrison capacity (`obj_max`, `+0x5d4`, the `.dat`'s `garrison_capacity`): how many\nunits an object of it holds; a building of any takes a gather point (`FUN_140e7e9a0`). Every\nbyte the data or an effect leaves is kept." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && 0 <= x && x <= 255),
  GarrisonKinds | doc "The set's flag names joined by ` | `, unnamed bits as one hexadecimal number (`0x10`)." = String,
  GarrisonTuning | doc "The `garrison` port's tuning values." = {
    enter_hp_share | Number | doc "The share of its master's hit points at or below which a building takes no unit that enters it (state 13; `DAT_142eae8d0`).\n\n`garrison::ENTER_HP_SHARE`: 0.2 in build 158041.",
    enter_near | Number | doc "How near the point a transport must reach for an Enter (slot 0x3d8's range), and the range up to which an Enter's reach of a target with speed tests the tiles about the two (`FUN_140a85c30`): `DAT_14330eb8c`, 1.0.\n\n`garrison::ENTER_NEAR`: 1 in build 158041.",
    least_hp_share | Number | doc "A building takes units in only above this share of its master's hit points (`FUN_14120eb10`, in doubles).\n\n`garrison::LEAST_HP_SHARE`: 0.2 in build 158041.",
    nearby | Number | doc "The squared footprint gap within which a garrison order's target's neighbours shelter units too (`FUN_14161e370` with `+0x1e`, `DAT_14330ebcc`, 100.0: ten tiles).\n\n`garrison::NEARBY`: 100 in build 158041.",
    rate_range | Number | doc "A combat master's attack rate needs a weapon range above this (`FUN_14120dc10`).\n\n`garrison::RATE_RANGE`: 1 in build 158041.",
    town_bell_reach | Number | doc "The squared footprint gap within which the town bell reaches (its ring `FUN_14163a650`, its end `FUN_14163ab80`, and `FUN_141621220` with `param_6` 1: `DAT_142ef3e70`, 625.0, 25 tiles).\n\n`garrison::TOWN_BELL_REACH`: 625 in build 158041.",
    unload_range | Number | doc "UNLOAD's order range (`DAT_14330eb8c`).\n\n`garrison::UNLOAD_RANGE`: 1 in build 158041.",
  },
  GatherGroup | doc "A master's gather group (`+0x683`, the `.dat`'s `resource_gather_group`): the kind of\nresource an object that gathers by itself (`enable_auto_gather`) offers, by which the unit\nAI's resource searches (`ClosestResourceObject`, `genie_core::unit_ai::ResourceSearch`) and the\nplayers' visible resources group the objects. The civilian's slot 0x1b0 gives one by a\ntarget's class (`genie_core::unit_ai::civilian_kind`), the work's search by a resource held\n(`genie_core::gathering::gather_search::gather_group`). The `.dat` may hold others, so the\ngroup is a newtype with named constants." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && 0 <= x && x <= 255),
  GatherSearchTuning | doc "The `gather_search` port's tuning values." = {
    diagonal | Number | doc "A pass's distance counts the shorter axis times this, rounded down, less the shorter one (`DAT_142efe414`).\n\n`gather_search::DIAGONAL`: 1.4 in build 158041.",
    reach_cap | Number | doc "The most reach a builder's search for more work takes from the building's line of sight (`DAT_142e7f38c`).\n\n`gather_search::REACH_CAP`: 20 in build 158041.",
    reach_floor | Number | doc "A building's line of sight below this gives a builder's search for more work its least reach (`DAT_142eb0f48`).\n\n`gather_search::REACH_FLOOR`: 4 in build 158041.",
    site_share | Number | doc "The search's centre between a drop site and the unit: the site's share (`DAT_142e7f388`).\n\n`gather_search::SITE_SHARE`: 0.75 in build 158041.",
    unit_share | Number | doc "The search's centre between a drop site and the unit: the unit's share (`DAT_142eb880c`).\n\n`gather_search::UNIT_SHARE`: 0.25 in build 158041.",
  },
  GatherTuning | doc "The `gather` port's tuning values." = {
    default_productivity | Number | doc "The productivity of a task without a productivity attribute (`DAT_14330eb8c`).\n\n`gather::DEFAULT_PRODUCTIVITY`: 1 in build 158041.",
    drop_reach | Number | doc "A drop-off reaches its drop site within this squared footprint gap (`DAT_14330eb8c`).\n\n`gather::DROP_REACH`: 1 in build 158041.",
    stop_centre | Number | doc "A stop's point lies this far into its tile (`DAT_142e7f384`).\n\n`gather::STOP_CENTRE`: 0.5 in build 158041.",
    wait_gap | Number | doc "A failed walk to a target at least this far away waits (the squared footprint gap, `0x140a8e1d0` case 3, `DAT_142ec9ec0`); else the gatherer searches.\n\n`gather::WAIT_GAP`: 16 in build 158041.",
    wait_shift | Number | doc "A random wait's shift (`DAT_142e7f384`).\n\n`gather::WAIT_SHIFT`: 0.5 in build 158041.",
    wait_workers | Number | doc "A failed walk to a target with at most this many workers waits (`0x140a8e1d0` case 3, `DAT_142eb1c98`); else the gatherer searches.\n\n`gather::WAIT_WORKERS`: 3 in build 158041.",
  },
  GhostMode | doc "A master's `create_doppelganger_on_death` (`+0x682`): whether its dying objects leave ghosts in\nthe other players' fog. Every byte is kept; only 2 leaves them." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && 0 <= x && x <= 255),
  Graphic | doc "What the clock reads of a sprite (the `.dat` graphic, memory `+0x8`..`+0x1a`)." = {
