    gaia_target_reach | Number | doc "A Gaia target lets the siege unit's range grow by this (`DAT_142eb4838`).\n\n`unit_ai::GAIA_TARGET_REACH`: 1.5 in build 158041.",
    harmless_hp | Number | doc "The hit points below which a villager fights its attacker back (`DAT_14330ebc8`).\n\n`unit_ai::HARMLESS_HP`: 60 in build 158041.",
    harmless_range | Number | doc "The range below which a villager fights its attacker back (`DAT_142e7f384`).\n\n`unit_ai::HARMLESS_RANGE`: 0.5 in build 158041.",
    help_reach | Number | doc "`AskForHelp`'s reach (`DAT_142ecccc4`): the squared footprint gap of 3 tiles.\n\n`unit_ai::HELP_REACH`: 9 in build 158041.",
    lion_sight_divisor | Number | doc "Finding no villager outside mode 1 it attacks within its line of sight over this (`FUN_140c1fb70`, `DAT_142eb1c98`).\n\n`unit_ai::LION_SIGHT_DIVISOR`: 3 in build 158041.",
    lion_sight_share | Number | doc "Outside mode 1 the lion attacks within this share of its line of sight (`FUN_140c1fb70`, `DAT_142e7f384`).\n\n`unit_ai::LION_SIGHT_SHARE`: 0.5 in build 158041.",
    never_killed | Number | doc "The damage case's kill time of an object the unit cannot harm (`DAT_142efe41c`, 25000).\n\n`unit_ai::NEVER_KILLED`: 25000 in build 158041.",
    patrol_turn_reach | Number | doc "A patrol's path goes back and forth when its point is at least this far from the unit (`0x140aa2a70`, `DAT_142eb1c98`).\n\n`unit_ai::PATROL_TURN_REACH`: 3 in build 158041.",
    radius_scale | Number | doc "The notify's radii are hundredths (`DAT_14330ebcc`).\n\n`unit_ai::RADIUS_SCALE`: 100 in build 158041.",
    retarget_range | Number | doc "A human player's unit on the attack order with a range above this does not retarget (processMisc).\n\n`unit_ai::RETARGET_RANGE`: 3 in build 158041.",
    retarget_reach | Number | doc "The retarget's reference distance about a current target (`DAT_142eb9430`).\n\n`unit_ai::RETARGET_REACH`: 8 in build 158041.",
    run_leash | Number | doc "`runAwayFromAttackers` (`FUN_140c5e900`): a defensive unit runs at most this far from its state position (`DAT_14330ebb8`).\n\n`unit_ai::RUN_LEASH`: 5 in build 158041.",
    run_reach | Number | doc "`runAwayFromAttackers` (`FUN_140c5e900`): the run is the unit's speed times this (`DAT_142e8c150`).\n\n`unit_ai::RUN_REACH`: 2 in build 158041.",
    ship_evade_reach | Number | doc "A computer player's ship evades the object its idle check found by its speed times this (`FUN_140c21930`, `FUN_140c1eab0`: `DAT_142ec9eb8`).\n\n`unit_ai::SHIP_EVADE_REACH`: 7 in build 158041.",
    single_volley | Number | doc "A building on its make action without a missile and with at most this firepower forgets its target (`DAT_14330eb8c`).\n\n`unit_ai::SINGLE_VOLLEY`: 1 in build 158041.",
    stance_range_growth | Number | doc "The soldier's range against a target grows by this for its stance checks (`DAT_142e7f384`).\n\n`unit_ai::STANCE_RANGE_GROWTH`: 0.5 in build 158041.",
    stand_ground_patrol_leash | Number | doc "Stand ground's leash from a saved patrol's path (`DAT_142e7f384`, 0.5).\n\n`unit_ai::STAND_GROUND_PATROL_LEASH`: 0.5 in build 158041.",
    stand_ground_slack | Number | doc "What the stand ground stance's leash adds to the unit's range (`DAT_142eb880c`, 0.25, read by `ADDSS` at `0x140c57c6a`).\n\n`unit_ai::STAND_GROUND_SLACK`: 0.25 in build 158041.",
  },
  UnitLines | doc "The two tables and the identifiers' list (`DAT_143f15808`: each line's identifiers with its\nid). Empty, as the game's when the file is missing, until [`UnitLines::build`]." = {
    entries | Array (LineEntry) | doc "Table 1, by master id.",
    firsts | Array (MasterId) | doc "Table 2, by line + 399: the line's first master (none, the game's −1).",
    identifiers | Array (Array Dyn) | doc "The identifiers, with their line, in the file's order.",
  },
  UpgradeMode | doc "An upgrade effect's mode (its third argument, `FUN_141657d10`'s): 2 changes the effect's\nown object alone, −1 and 3 keep the objects' masters, 3 also takes the objects whose own\nmaster has the upgraded master's id; any other walks the objects and gives them masters\nof their own." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && -32768 <= x && x <= 32767),
  VanishMode | doc "The set's flag names joined by ` | `, unnamed bits as one hexadecimal number (`0x10`)." = String,
  VisibilityTuning | doc "The `visibility` port's tuning values." = {
    edge | Number | doc "`DAT_142eb99cc`: a footprint's high edge, less this, is its last tile.\n\n`visibility::EDGE`: 0.01 in build 158041.",
  },
  VolleySpread | doc "A master's `volley_x_spread`, `volley_y_spread` and `volley_start_spread_adjustment`\n(`+0x8c8`..`+0x8d0`, the `.dat`'s projectile spawning area): how far a volley's missiles\nscatter across and along the shot, and how far forward they start." = {
    x | Distance | doc "`volley_x_spread` (`+0x8c8`, the attribute \"Spawning Area Width\").",
    y | Distance | doc "`volley_y_spread` (`+0x8cc`, \"Spawning Area Length\").",
    start | Distance | doc "`volley_start_spread_adjustment` (`+0x8d0`, \"Spawning Area Randomness\").",
  },
  WaitSolidifyTuning | doc "The `wait_solidify` port's tuning values." = {
    solid_from | Number | doc "`DAT_142eb56a0` (a double): the foundation's build points (`+0xc50`, widened) at most which it is not solid yet.\n\n`wait_solidify::SOLID_FROM`: 0.01 in build 158041.",
  },
  WallTuning | doc "The `wall` port's tuning values." = {
    map_margin | Number | doc "How far inside the map's far edges the snap keeps a footprint (`FUN_141123ac0`).\n\n`wall::MAP_MARGIN`: 0.00001 in build 158041.",
  },
  WholeSeconds | doc "A build, train or research time in whole seconds as a master's or a technology's data holds it\n(a short: a master's `+0x898` train locations, its build time): every short is kept, and\n[`Seconds::of_master`] is the game's conversion." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && -32768 <= x && x <= 32767),
  WorkRate | doc "The work an object does per second, as the game's `f32` holds it: a master's `work_rate`\n(`+0x798`) and an object's powerup of it (`mWorkRatePowerup`, `+0xa30`, slot 0x6e8), their\nsum as a gatherer, a hunter, a builder, a repairer, a farm or a producing building works.\nA task's work value scales it ([`WorkRate`] times an `f32`), and over [`Seconds`] it is the\nwork done, in the task's own unit (an amount, build or repair points, training progress).\nEach operator is the one `f32` operation the game does, in its order; a comparison is\n`f32`'s (a NaN compares false)." = Number,
  WorkValue | doc "A task's work value (`work_val1`, `+0x28`, and `work_val2`, `+0x2c`, floats of the `.dat`):\nwhat its action reads by its type. A gather's and a build's `work_val1` scales the worker's\nwork rate, a generation's the attribute it grows, a movement damage's the hit points it takes\nand its `work_val2` the seconds between; a task whose `work_val1` is at most 0 is no target's\n(the task finder). Every value is kept." = Number,
  WorkerCount | doc "A count of workers: the actions that have an object as their target (`worker_num`,\n`+0x644`: a farm's farmer, a resource's gatherers, a building's builders), and a cap on\nthem (a drop site's target's `worker_num`, a search's argument, [`WorkerCount::NO_CAP`]\nfor none). Every value is kept." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0),
  WorldPlayerTuning | doc "The `world_player` port's tuning values." = {
    livestock_scale | Number | doc "The livestock food over which a mill's yield grows by one e-fold (`DAT_142eb0f54`).\n\n`world_player::LIVESTOCK_SCALE`: 200 in build 158041.",
  },
}
